  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id) not stated.\n(b_no_id_remedy)\n(section) Sec. 6, 2-2-111(f) (new)\n(quote) A registration form from a person who registers to vote at a supplemental registration who does not present evidence of identification or verification of residential address, as those terms are defined in § 2-7-112, must be processed in accordance with § 2-2-115.\n(section) Sec. 2, 2-7-112(a)(3)(B)(i) (added sentence)\n(quote) The county election commission shall publish a notice of the location of the provisional counting board in conjunction with the notice of election required by § 2-12-111(c) and shall not change the location except in the event of an emergency.\n(section) Sec. 1, 2-7-112(e)(10)\n(quote) If the county election commission determines that the counting of provisional ballots cannot be completed by the designated time, the state coordinator of elections may grant the county an extension of time and shall designate a time that is no later than the third Monday after the election.\n(c_mail_ballot_id) not stated.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship) not stated.\n(e_other_rule)\n(section) Sec. 5, 2-2-118(a)\n(quote) A person who registers to vote in the county election commission office shall present evidence of identification or verification of residential address, as those terms are defined in § 2-7-112.\n(section) Sec. 7, 2-2-124(a)\n(quote) The administrator of elections shall mail the voter registration card to any new voter who has not provided verification of residential address, as defined in § 2-7-112, or who registers at a supplemental registration held pursuant to § 2-2-111.\n(section) Sec. 3, 2-9-110(d)-(e)\n(quote) The county election commission shall not tabulate any marked ballots submitted via the internet. (e) Voting machines are prohibited from being connected to the internet.\n(other) Sec. 4, 2-2-106(c)(2): address-change process also used when a voter has not voted or updated registration over two consecutive regular November elections.\n(other) Sec. 8, 2-2-132: purge of permanent registration records of persons required to be purged under 2-2-106, unless federal law bars it.\n(other) Sec. 9: effective on becoming law (signed 2025-05-05).\n(other) version: 3093364-Draft: caption bill; amends 2-5-151(c) so the commission may notify petition filers of a defect in documentation. No slot a-e text.\n(other) version: amend-244716-SA0305 (Senate State & Local Gov't amendment 1; 'adopted' flag 0 but action log shows adoption on 2025-04-09): deletes all after the enacting clause; substitutes Secs. 1-9 above, adding the slot b and e text.\n(other) version: 3235585-Chaptered (PC 371): same as SA0305 (PDF text damaged in places; SA0305 is the clean copy).\n(other) note: Quotes are taken from SA0305 because the chaptered PDF text is garbled in Secs. 5-6; the two are the same wording. This bill adds no new ID rule to vote in person; it connects the existing 2-7-112 terms 'evidence of identification' and 'verification of residential address' to registration at the commission office and at supplemental registrations. Same enacted text as the House companion HB0457. All three recorded roll calls were on Draft + SA0305, so the voted text DOES carry slot b/e text although the filed Draft has none.",
